  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure will slowly build over the region today shifting\nto the east by Sunday. This will lead to mostly clear and dry\nweather with much less wind compared to Friday. Near normal \nhigh temperatures today will trend a few degrees above normal on\nSunday as flow turns south to southwesterly. Temperatures\nwill be falling into the 40s for most areas during trick-or-\ntreating time this evening with values lowering into the 30s \nacross the Adirondacks. This high should remain just off the \ncoast to bring mainly dry weather early next week as well. \nHowever, a few showers along a northward lifting warm front may \nbrush portions of the Adirondacks on Tuesday. High temperatures \nMonday through Wednesday will be mainly in the 60s which is 10 \nto 15 degrees above normal. The next best chance for some rain \ncontinues to be later next week, though there continues to be \nsignificant model differences into how the overall synoptic \npattern evolves. Solution continue to vary from just a few \nshowers to a potentially widespread soaking rain. Trends will \ncontinue to be monitored over the next several days.",
